{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - 1.\tThe proposed new dwelling, by reason of its position, size, height, depth and position close to the boundaries of the site, a design with a roof garden and an ASHP without noise assessment, would be an intrusive, inappropriate and unneighbourly development to the area, failing to maintain and enhance the appearance and character of the street, have a serious and adverse effect on the amenities enjoyed by adjoining residents causing loss of daylight and sunlight, privacy, overbearing appearance with a sense of enclosure, thus contrary to Local Plan policies CC1; CC2; CC4; SC7, London Plan policy D4, and the intent of the National Planning Policy Framework and Housing SPG.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal makes no justification of a single aspect unit and so would be detrimental to the amenities enjoyed by prospective occupants of this development in terms of receiving sufficient sunlight/daylight and having cross ventilation as well as being out of character with the prevailing pattern of the development in the surrounding area contrary to Local Plan policies CC1; CC2; SC5, London Plan policy D6, and the intent of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposal, due to the lack of fire safety information, would be contrary to London Plan policy D12 and the intent of the National Planning Policy Framework."
  ],
